(*!
<summary>Beckhoff EL3413/EL3433 auxiliary measurement input PDO.</summary>
<description>
Represents TxPDO 0x1A03 at 0x6030: Status WORD, acknowledged Index/Channel bytes and signed Value.
Status bit 2 reports overcurrent where supported, bit 14 invalidates data and bit 15 toggles on update.
Use Value only after both input selectors acknowledge the requested output selectors and status is valid.
Units and supported selector combinations depend on device/firmware; examples include neutral current,
energy totals and harmonics. This raw record performs no unit conversion or validity checking.
Link fields individually. Use one owner task and synchronize other access; snapshots are not atomic.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
</description>
*)
TYPE POWER_MEASUREMENT_AUXILIARY_INPUT_CHANNEL :
STRUCT
	Status AT %I* : WORD;
	Index AT %I* : USINT;
	Channel AT %I* : USINT;
	Value AT %I* : DINT;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
